\caption{(a) Permutation rule for the special term in eigenequation. A three-qubit system with an interaction $\mathcal{H}_0^3+\mathcal{H}_s^{3,1}$ is considered. Each permutation is denoted by a line starting from a nonzero off-diagonal element in the first row (denoted by colored arrows) and ending at a nonzero element in the last column. (b) For one example permutation, the term is composed by all circled elements. The sign of the permutation (e.g., 81325674) can be obtained from off-diagonal elements only, leading to $(-1)^n$.}
