\section{Shifted symplectic structures}

Let us now turn to the description of symplectic structures on Lie $n$-groupoids. The first components we need to define for this are tangent spaces and differential forms. But, whenever we are dealing with higher objects, we will have a tangent complex rather than a tangent space. In this case, symplectic structures can be shifted with respect to the grading of the tangent complex.
