\subsubsection{Preprocessing of raw data}
We preprocess the raw scRNA-seq data using an established method \cite{pratapa2020benchmarking} to handle redundancy. We filter out low-expressed genes and prioritized the variable ones. Primarily, the genes expressed in less than 10\% of cells were removed. Then, we computed the variance and P-values for each gene, selecting those with P-values below 0.01 after Bonferroni correction. Gene expression levels were log-transformed for normalization. This yielded a feature matrix \( \mathcal{X} \in \mathbb{R}^{N \times F} \), where \( N \) is the number of genes and \( F \) is the number of cells. Furthermore, we adopt the approach of Pratapa et al.\cite{pratapa2020benchmarking} to assess performance across different network sizes. Specifically, we rank genes by variance and select the most variable transcription factors (TFs), along with the top 500 and 1000 genes with the highest variability.

\subsection{Baseline methods}
We evaluate the efficacy of \emph{GT-GRN} against the existing baselines methods commonly used for inferring GRNs:

\begin{itemize}

    \item \textbf{GNNLink\cite{mao2023predicting}} uses GCN-based interaction graph encoder to capture gene expression patterns.

    \vspace{0.18cm}

    \item \textbf{GENELink\cite{chen2022graph}} levereges graph attention network (GAT) to infer GRNs via attention mechanisms.

    \vspace{0.18cm}


    \item \textbf{GNE \cite{kc2019gne}} uses a MLP (multi-layered perceptron) to encode gene expression profiles and network topology to predict the gene regulatory links.

    \vspace{0.18cm}


    \item \textbf{ARACNE\cite{margolin2006aracne}} infers network based on Adaptive Partioning (AP) and Mutual Information (MI) approach.

    \vspace{0.18cm}

    \item \textbf{BC3NET\cite{de2012bagging}} is an ensemble technique derived from the C3NET algorithm that employs a bagging approach for inferring GRNs.

    \vspace{0.18cm}


    \item \textbf{C3MTC} infers gene interaction network where the edge weights are defined by the corresponding mutual information values.

    \vspace{0.18cm}

    \item \textbf{C3NET\cite{altay2010inferring}} leverages mutual  information estimates and a maximization step to efficiently captures causal structural information in the data. 

    \vspace{0.18cm}

    \item \textbf{PPCOR\cite{kim2015ppcor}} calculates both partial and semi-partial correlation coefficients individually for every pair of genes.

    \vspace{0.18cm}


    \item \textbf{GRNBOOST2\cite{moerman2019grnboost2}} is a fast GRN inference algorithm using Stochastic Gradient Boosting Machine (SGBM) regression.

    \vspace{0.18cm}

    \item \textbf{GENIE3\cite{huynh2010inferring}} is a classic GRN inference algorithm using Random Forest (RF) or ExtraTrees (ET) regression.
\end{itemize}


