\subsection{Evaluation of EB estimators and MSE estimator}
We first evaluated the performance of six empirical Bayes (EB) estimators and the direct estimator, as follows:
\begin{description}
\item [(NBT.RE)]Natural back transformation with the REML estimator of $A$,  
\item [(NBT.YL)]Natural back transformation with the adjusted REML estimator of $A$ suggested by \cite{yoshimori2014} to avoid zero estimates.
\item [(pEB.RE)] EB estimator with the REML estimator of $A$ under the assumption $\theta_i=g(\mu_i)$,
\item [(pEB.YL)] EB estimator with the adjusted REML estimator of $A$ under the assumption $\theta_i=g(\mu_i)$,
\item [(EB.RE)] EB estimator with the REML estimator of $A$ under our new assumption based on \eqref{eq7.25312}, up to the order $O(n_i^{-1})$,
\item [(EB.YL)] EB estimator with the adjusted REML estimator of $A$ under our new assumption based on \eqref{eq7.25312}, up to the order $O(n_i^{-1})$,
\item[(Direct)] the direct estimator $y_i$. 
\end{description}

