\section{Final Remarks}
The paper introduces an asymptotically bias-corrected variance stabilizing transformation in the context of area-level small area models. 
In addition, we consider a scenario where not just the number of small areas is large, but also some of these areas have large or moderately large sample sizes. Theoretical result was found in this setup, and are accompanied with data analysis and simulation. An important new research will be to extend this variance stabilizing idea to unit level models with or without moderately large samples in a given unit. 




